in the marvel universe the eternal known  as icarus has been around for a very  long time hundreds of thousands of years  in fact but to many comic fans he's  still something of a mystery this is  everything you need to know about icarus  from eternals perhaps the most important  thing about icarus is that he isn't just  any other eternal he's a so-called prime  eternal but that hasn't always been the  case after the godlike cronus's fateful  experiments with cosmic energy leaves  his mind separated from his body his two  sons zorus and alas fight a conflict  over the future of the eternals when  zorus wins alas leaves for jupiter's  moon titan where he will later become  father to thanos then after the  remaining eternals form the collective  eternal consciousness known as the uni  mind it chooses zorus to be the prime  maternal zoros is later killed in battle  with the celestials and thena is  selected as the new prime maternal in  1986's eternals issue 9 after icarus  accuses teen of treason over her loyalty  to her deviant lover crow thiena passes  on the role of prime eternal to icarus  being the prime maternal means more than  getting a fancy title though among other  things whoever is named by maternal is  given the privilege of initiating the  formation of the  an act that has saved both the eternals  and earth on more than one occasion  icarus boasts a wide array of abilities  including impressive super strength and  durability he expertly wields cosmic  energy has often seen blasting from his  eyes and he can manipulate this ability  in various ways  unsurprisingly these powers serve him  well in battle in 1977's eternals issue  14 issue 15 icarus goes toe to toe with  a cosmic-powered robot designed to look  act and display powers similar to the  incredible hulk well not the real deal  the cosmic-powered hulk robot is no  pushover and on top of that icarus has  faced all kinds of similarly powerful  challenges over the years similar to the  other eternals icarus can fly and while  they aren't his most used abilities he's  also been shown to have both the  capacity to teleport and use some  low-level psychic powers  if you're familiar with the world of  ancient myth then you've probably  already guessed that the name icarus is  inspired by icarus the boy who flew too  close to the sun and in the mid-80s  marvel miniseries the connection between  icarus and icarus became much more  literal in greco-roman myth icarus is  the son of daedalus a genius forced by  king minos to design a labyrinth to  contain the terrifying minotaur when  king minos imprisons settlers and his  family so that the secret of the  labyrinth can never be revealed daedalus  constructs his own flying machines out  of bird feathers and wax upon their  escape daedalus wants his son not to fly  too close to the sun but icarus ignores  him and when the wax of icarus flying  contraption melts he plummets to his  death in 1986's eternals issue 5 is  revealed that in the marvel universe the  eternal icarus was actually the  inspiration for this story centuries ago  icarus had a son named icarus one day  believing his father to be imprisoned by  deviants icarus attempted to use a  mechanical flying device to find his  father like the icarus of myth the boy  flew too high and eventually fell to his  death after learning of his son's fate  the eternal named himself icarus to  honor his fallen child  one of the x-men's most infamous  villains is apocalypse who first shows  up using that name in 1986's x factor  issue 5. it's since been revealed that  apocalypse had faced a number of heroes  before he met any of the x-men however  for example he fought a younger thor in  2013's uncanny avengers issue six and at  one point he even faced off against  icarus and the eternals in the 2001 shot  new eternals apocalypse now the evil  mutant unleashes his latest sworded  scheme icarus some apocalypse don't meet  face to face until toward the end of the  story but when they do it's suggested  that they're actually old enemies the  details are left a little murky but  icarus refers to the villain as n  sabaner suggesting their last encounter  was centuries ago when apocalypse was  better known by that name icarus also  claims that he'd believed apocalypse had  died in their last meeting at first that  might not seem like much of a reveal  after all as a popular marvel comics  villain apocalypse is legally required  to die and be resurrected every few  years but the fact that icarus and his  brethren so thoroughly defeated  apocalypse as to believe him dead proves  just how formidable these heroes can be  who do you think's gonna lead the  avengers  i could lead them  [Music]  since the eternals tend to live separate  from humanity it's perhaps  understandable that some of them aren't  exactly thrilled to be sharing the earth  with humans consequently some eternals  aren't quite as dedicated to their  safekeeping as they should be icarus  however has always done everything he  can to defend humankind ever since  ancient times icarus has gone above and  beyond to protect the people of earth  from his guidance of noah's ark to  safety all the way up to his allegiance  with the avengers icarus has always  advocated for the humans despite having  advanced beyond them in many ways this  is why when most of the eternals leave  earth after their battle with the  inhuman villain maelstrom it cares as  one of the few selected by the uni mind  to stay behind and continue to use his  powers to protect those who can't  protect themselves  the idea of a superhero taking on a  relatively mundane job is nothing new  spider-man has been a photographer  daredevil has been a lawyer and the  god-like superman has enjoyed a thriving  career as a reporter for the daily  planet regardless it still feels like  kind of a shock that the 1985 eternals  miniseries finds a noble and powerful  icarus working as a professional  wrestler in 1985's eternals issue 1 it  becomes apparent that icarus has joined  the ranks of marvel's unlimited class  wrestling federation as ike at the  iceberg harris the issue even shows him  in action in his wrestling dicks and  judging by the applause and cheers this  is hardly iceberg's first time in the  rink of course it's eventually revealed  icarus didn't join the ucwf because he  enjoys hitting people with folding  chests in fact icarus has been climbing  the ucwf's ranks for the chance to take  on the wrestler enigma who's actually  cataphracts the mighty a deviant villain  in disguise the ucwf was one of the more  prominent marvel fictional organizations  in the 1980s along with icarus a number  of other heroes have joined and wrestled  in the ucwf though the most prominent  was none other than ben grimm  icarus and the other eternals claimed  the distinction of starring in one of  the few comic books that neil gaiman has  written for marvel comics comic book  wise gaiman is best known for his  groundbreaking dc vertigo sandman series  though he's written a few projects for  marvel 2. in 2003 he wrote 1602 which  introduced early 17th century european  versions of most of marvel's most  popular heroes then after marvel  acquired the rights to miracle man  gaiman wrote subsequent issues for the  long lost character and in 2006 he  teamed up with the legendary artist john  romita jr to bring to life another  dormant property the eternals the  mid-earth's eternals mini-series begins  with each of the godlike beings stripped  of their memories and living as ordinary  humans the speedster makari for example  is living as mark curry a med student  cersei is a party organizer athena is a  scientist working for stark industries  and zorus is an alcoholic homeless man  it's eventually revealed that their  memories have been stripped by the  mischievous sprites but before that  becomes clear it's icarus who sets out  to find the eternals and reawaken their  old memories  a few years later the eternals fell to a  horrible fate and icarus was the last of  them to survive when avengers relaunched  in 2018 it was led by a storyline  involving the dark celestials a group of  evil cosmic beings after the corpses of  the true celestials fall to earth the  avenger sets out on a quest that  ultimately reveals a dark secret about  the eternals humanity and the celestials  themselves when iron man travels to the  eternal's home of olympus hoping to get  some more information about what has  happened he instead finds a massacre the  only living eternal he finds is icarus  and even then the prime eternal doesn't  survive for long icarus stays alive just  long enough to reveal that his people  erupted into madness when they learn  their true purpose essentially the dark  celestials meant for humanity to act as  a virus against an army of insects like  monsters called the horde and the  eternals were meant to cultivate that  virus and get humanity ready for the  harvesting before he succumbs his wounds  icarus gives iron man access to the uni  mind which the avengers are later able  to use to defeat the dark celestials in  2021 the eternals returned for the fifth  volume of their eponymous series this  story finds icarus and is a mortal  compatriot brought back from the dead  they are eternal after all set loose in  a battle against thanos icarus is killed  and rebirthed again and only then  discovers the horrible truth of the  eternal's immortality that they're  resurrected at the cost of human lives  unable to end this process without  endangering the earth the eternal set  out to solve their problem leading them  into a fragile alliance with their old  enemies the deviants  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  marvel comics are coming soon subscribe  to our youtube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

